---
import { DOCS } from "../config"
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro"
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "")
---
<Base title="Witnesses" description="The witnesses who confirm Mene advisories, what each has confirmed, and how to become one.">
  <section class="panel flat page-head">
    <div class="wrap center">
      <h1>Witnesses</h1>
      <p class="lede">Witnesses are the security teams whose confirmations count. An advisory blocks installs only when 2 of these 3 witnesses confirm it, so no single account can fake or hide a warning.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="wrap">

    <div id="cards" class="wgrid"><div class="sk"></div><div class="sk"></div><div class="sk"></div></div>

    <section class="card how">
      <h2>Choose whose confirmations count</h2>
      <p>Today's witnesses are three testnet wallets run by the Mene team; in production they would be independent security organisations. You decide which witnesses you trust wherever you run Mene:</p>
      <div class="two">
        <div>
          <p class="small muted">CLI: <code>mene.config.json</code> in your project</p>
<pre><code id="cfg">{`{
  "issuers": ["0x…", "0x…", "0x…"],
  "threshold": 2,
  "minSeverity": "low"
}`}</code></pre>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="small muted">GitHub Action inputs (or use the <a href={`${base}/setup`}>setup builder</a>)</p>
<pre><code>- uses: andrew1234-arch/mene@v1
  with:
    lockfile: package-lock.json
    issuers: 0x…,0x…,0x…
    threshold: 2</code></pre>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="card how become">
      <h2>Become a witness</h2>
      <p>A witness is a wallet that publishes and confirms advisories. It needs a funded Tiramisu testnet key (see the <a href="https://docs.arkiv.network/networks/tiramisu/">faucet</a>) kept in an environment variable, never in a file.</p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Publish</strong> an advisory in OSV format. It is written so it can't be edited and sealed so it can't be deleted:
<pre><code>{`export MENE_ISSUER_KEY=0x…        # your witness key, from a secret store
npx mene-check publish advisory.osv.json`}</code></pre></li>
        <li><strong>Confirm</strong> (or withdraw) an advisory another witness published:
<pre><code>{`npx mene-check attest 0xADVISORY_KEY --confirm
npx mene-check attest 0xADVISORY_KEY --withdraw --reason "false positive"`}</code></pre></li>
        <li><strong>Ask to be trusted.</strong> Users add your address to their witness list. Publish your address on a page you control so they can check it's yours.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="small muted">Witnesses with a browser wallet can also confirm or withdraw from any advisory's “Verify this advisory” panel. <a href={DOCS.cli}>CLI reference →</a></p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style is:global>
  .wgrid { display: grid; gap: .8rem; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr)); margin: 1.5rem 0 2rem; }
  .wgrid .sk { height: 140px; }
  .wcard { display: grid; gap: .45rem; align-content: start; }
  .wcard h3 { margin: 0; }
  .wcard dl { display: grid; grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr; gap: .2rem .8rem; margin: .2rem 0 0; font-size: .9rem; }
  .wcard dt { color: var(--muted); }
  .wcard dd { margin: 0; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .how .two { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr)); gap: 1rem; }
  .how .two > div { min-width: 0; }
  .become { margin-top: 1.2rem; }
  .become ol { display: grid; gap: .8rem; padding-left: 1.2rem; }
  .become pre { margin: .5rem 0 0; }
</style>

<script>
  import { addrHtml, errorHtml, esc, getTrust, link, watchWall } from "../scripts/mene"

  const cards = document.getElementById("cards")!
  const t = getTrust()
  if (t.issuers.length) {
    document.getElementById("cfg")!.textContent = JSON.stringify({ issuers: t.issuers.map((i) => i.address), threshold: t.threshold, minSeverity: "low" }, null, 2)
  }

  watchWall(
    (wall) => {
      cards.innerHTML = t.issuers
        .map((i) => {
          const a = i.address.toLowerCase()
          const inscribed = wall.statuses.filter((s) => s.advisory?.creator === a).length
          const verdicts = wall.statuses.flatMap((s) => s.witnesses.filter((w) => w.issuer === a))
          const confirms = verdicts.filter((v) => v.verdict === "confirm").length
          const withdraws = verdicts.filter((v) => v.verdict === "withdraw").length
          const last = Math.max(0, ...verdicts.map((v) => v.createdAt))
          return `<div class="card wcard">
            <h3>${esc(i.name || "Witness")}</h3>
            <div>${addrHtml(i.address)}</div>
            <dl>
              <dt>Published</dt><dd>${inscribed}</dd>
              <dt>Confirmed</dt><dd>${confirms}</dd>
              <dt>Withdrawn</dt><dd>${withdraws}</dd>
              <dt>Last verdict</dt><dd>${last ? `block ${last}` : "—"}</dd>
            </dl>
            ${(() => {
              const ids = wall.statuses.filter((st) => st.witnesses.some((v) => v.issuer === a && v.verdict === "confirm")).map((st) => st.advisory?.osv.id).filter(Boolean) as string[]
              return ids.length ? `<p class="small muted">Confirmed: ${ids.slice(0, 6).map((x) => `<a href="${link("advisories", { id: x })}">${esc(x)}</a>`).join(", ")}${ids.length > 6 ? ` and ${ids.length - 6} more` : ""}</p>` : ""
            })()}
          </div>`
        })
        .join("")
    },
    (err, retry) => {
      cards.innerHTML = errorHtml(err)
      cards.querySelector("[data-retry]")?.addEventListener("click", retry)
    },
  )
</script>
